@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy | ksamods.gg</PageTitle>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated 8 August 2026.</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <section>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Short version: you can browse this site without an account and without being
                tracked. If you sign in, we store what we need to know who you are and keep
                you signed in. Nothing beyond that.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Browsing without an account</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                No account, no cookie, no analytics, no third-party scripts. We don't build a
                profile of what you looked at.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
                One thing worth knowing: mod banner images are hosted by the mod authors, not by
                us. Loading a page with a banner on it makes your browser fetch that image from
                wherever the author put it, which means that host can see the request. We ask
                your browser not to send a referrer along with it, so they learn much less than
                they otherwise would, but the request still happens.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">If you sign in</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                Signing in uses GitHub or Discord. We never see your password, and we don't ask
                either service for more than we need. What we keep:
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-muted-foreground">
                <li>Your handle and display name, because they appear on your listings.</li>
                <li>Your account id at the provider you signed in with, so we recognise you next time.</li>
                <li>Your avatar URL, if the provider gave us one.</li>
                <li>Your KSA forums thread, if you add one. That one is public by design.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Sessions</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                A session is a row in our database, not a self-contained token, which means we
                can actually revoke it when you sign out. Against that row we store when it was
                issued, when it expires, your browser's user agent string, and a hash of your IP
                address.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
                The IP is hashed, never written down in the clear. We use it to spot abuse and to
                rate limit, not to work out where you live.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
                The session cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax, so JavaScript on the page can't
                read it and other sites can't borrow it. It's the only cookie we set, and it
                exists solely to keep you signed in.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">What we publish</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                Mod metadata, including your handle as its author, goes into a public exported
                index and a public git mirror. That's the point of the site: the data is meant
                to outlive us and be readable by other clients. Assume anything attached to a
                listing is public and permanent, because copies of that export will end up in
                places we don't control.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Deleting your account</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                Ask and we'll remove your account and its sessions. Listings are harder: other
                people's modlists may pin them, and the exported index has already been copied
                elsewhere. We can unlist your mods and detach them from you, but we can't
                retract snapshots other people have taken.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            @* TODO: contact channel, same as Terms. A privacy policy with no route to a human is
               not one, and deletion requests have to land somewhere. *@
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Getting in touch</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                Questions about any of this, or a request to delete your account, go to the
                moderators. Ask and we'll tell you exactly what we hold about you.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>
